  "historical_output_text": " How to Prepare a Raised Garden Bed for Planting\n\n1. **Choose a Suitable Location:** Place your raised garden bed in a sunny area that receives at least 6-8 hours of direct sunlight daily. This ensures your plants get the necessary light for photosynthesis. Avoid areas with strong winds, as these can damage plants and soil.\n\n2. **Clear the Ground:** Remove any grass, weeds, or debris from the area where you'll place your bed. This prevents competition with your plants and makes it easier to level the ground.\n\n3. **Assemble the Bed:** If you are using pre-made kits or building your own, assemble the bed according to the manufacturer's instructions or your design plan. Raised beds enhance soil drainage and prevent weeds from spreading.\n\n4. **Add a Layer of Compost:** Spread a layer of compost (about 2-3 inches thick",
